# SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-or-later
# The home (Sam, 2026-11-13: "expose the favorite home screen in the global settings ... default to simple"): boot
# shows the splash, then the home, on a fresh device the now-playing screen (Settings' HOME SCREEN SIMPLE). HOME on
# now playing or the main screen switches between the two but leaves the home as it is; only Settings' HOME SCREEN
# (its third line, any of K1-K4) changes it: DETAILED, the main screen. The home is where boot, a new song and HOME
# from elsewhere land; the device keeps it through a reboot. A change while a song plays is kept only once all is
# silent (stopped, the tails over): a flash save stalls the audio (a crackle, Sam 2026-11-11).
listen
expect splash 1
wait 1400
expect splash 0
expect home_now 1
expect home 1
shot home-now.png
# HOME: the main screen, the home still now playing; HOME again: back
tap HOME
wait 50
expect home_now 1
expect home 0
tap HOME
wait 50
expect home 1
# HOME on the main screen, then GLO, then HOME: the home, now playing
tap HOME
tap GLO
wait 50
said HOME SCREEN SIMPLE
tap HOME
wait 50
expect home 1
expect home_now 1
# Settings: HOME SCREEN DETAILED; GLO back lands on the new home, kept at once (stopped)
tap GLO
wait 50
spin SELECT 2
turn K1 1
wait 50
said HOME SCREEN DETAILED
expect home_now 0
tap GLO
wait 50
expect home 1
expect home_kept 1
reboot
expect splash 1
wait 1400
expect home_now 0
expect home 1
# while a song plays: back to SIMPLE (an even number of detents: no change), kept only once stopped
tap PLAY
wait 3000
tap GLO
wait 50
spin SELECT 2
turn K3 2
wait 50
expect home_now 0
turn K4 -1
wait 50
said HOME SCREEN SIMPLE
expect home_now 1
wait 2000
expect home_kept 0
tap HOME
wait 50
expect home 1
shot home-now-playing.png
# HOME: the main screen; a new song lands on the home, now playing
tap HOME
wait 50
expect home 0
tap SEQ
wait 3000
expect home 1
tap PLAY
wait 2000
expect home_kept 1
reboot
wait 1400
expect home_now 1
expect home 1
